# Phase Omega: Grand Verification (Design Journal)

> **Date:** 2026-01-11
> **Topic:** End-to-End System Verification (Phases 0-12)
> **Status:** In Progress
> **Authors:** Antigravity & User

---

## 1. Executive Summary
This journal documents "Project Omega", a synthetic initiative designed to exercise every layer of the Nucleus architecture in a single continuous flow.

**The Core Problem:**
We have built multiple powerful subsystems (Brain, Coder, Critic, Sensory), but they have mostly been tested in isolation or in pairs. We lack definitive proof that the entire organism functions coherently.

**The Solution:**
Design and execute a "Grand Verification Protocol" where a single feature ("Omega") flows from intent (Phase 0) to strategy (Phase 2), coding (Phase 3), review (Phase 12), and sensory verification (Phase 4-7).

---

## 2. Architectural Evolution

### 2.1 The "Grand Loop"
**Concept:**
Instead of unit tests, we perform a "Lifecycle Test".

**Key Decisions:**
*   **Synthetic Feature:** We chose a throwaway feature ("Omega") to avoid polluting the core product with test artifacts.
*   **Sequential vs Parallel:** We execute sequentially to prove dependencies (Strategy -> Code -> Review) work as expected.

---

## 3. Technical Deep Dives

### 3.1 The Critic Integration
**The Critical Hurdle:**
Ensuring the Critic Agent (Phase 12) can parse and review the code generated by the Coder Agent (Phase 3) without human intervention.

**The Solution:**
*   **Code Snippet:** Using [brain_critique_code](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#4473-4485) tool.
*   **Why:** Demonstrates AI-to-AI handoff (Coder -> Critic).

---

## 5. Conclusion
If successful, this journal serves as the "Proof of Life" for Nucleus v0.5.0.

---
